\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Zero-overlap PFA cancellation and 3D rotational clutch architecture in vacuum ($\varepsilon _{\rm  bg}=1.0$).} \textbf  {a}, Two-dimensional cross-sectional schematic comparing Euclidean parallel plates ($A_{\rm  overlap} > 0$, dominated by attractive proximity-force scaling $F_z^{\rm  PFA} \propto -A_{\rm  overlap}/d^4$), uniform periodic slot-tooth interdigitation ($A_{\rm  overlap} = 0$, limited by single-scale evanescent screening at $\kappa \sim \pi /W_0$), and prefractal Cantor interdigitation ($W_k = W_1 b^{-(k-1)}$, stepped depths $H_k$, partitioning transverse fringing fields across separated wavenumber bands). \textbf  {b}, Three-dimensional cutaway render of the four-fold symmetric ($C_4$, $90^\circ $ sector period) concentric gold rotor and stator in the disengaged open-slot state ($\theta = 3^\circ $). Downward-protruding concentric rotor teeth ($z \in [-100, 0]\text  { nm}$, $H_1 = 100{}\text  { nm}$, $H_2 = 90{}\text  { nm}$) interdigitate radially inside thin slotted Cantor stator aperture rings ($25\text  { nm}$ membrane thickness, $z \in [-25, 0]\text  { nm}$) suspended above recessed azimuthal landing pads ($150\text  { nm}$ thickness, top surface at $z = -115\text  { nm}$) and supported by a four-spoke $\text  {Si}\langle 110\rangle $ flexure suspension. \textbf  {c},\textbf  {d}, Cutaway renders and axial-radial $(r,z)$ cross-sections in (\textbf  {c}) the disengaged open-slot state ($\theta = 0^\circ \text  {--}6^\circ $, $A_{\rm  overlap} = 0$, $F_z^{\rm  PFA} = 0$, showing upward saddle-point repulsive force $F_z = +\roundtwo  {3.17743}\text  { pN}$ at $z_{\rm  tip} = -100\text  { nm}$ for $N=3$ on the \texttt  {Standard} BEM mesh) and (\textbf  {d}) the engaged landing-pad state ($\theta = 18^\circ \text  {--}48^\circ $, $A_{\rm  overlap} > 0$ across the $d = 15\text  { nm}$ vertical gap, showing normal attraction $F_z = \roundtwo  {-14.0388}\text  { pN}$ for $N=3$). \textbf  {e}, Radial cross-sectional profiles comparing the single-track baseline ($N=0$), first-generation slot ($N=1$), uniform periodic and monotonic controls, stepped $(r,z)$ $N=2$ Cantor ring, and seven-track $N=3$ Cantor ring across $r \in [0.30, 1.65]\ \mu \text  {m}$.}}{5}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:rotational_clutch_architecture}{{1}{5}{\textbf {Zero-overlap PFA cancellation and 3D rotational clutch architecture in vacuum ($\varepsilon _{\rm bg}=1.0$).} \textbf {a}, Two-dimensional cross-sectional schematic comparing Euclidean parallel plates ($A_{\rm overlap} > 0$, dominated by attractive proximity-force scaling $F_z^{\rm PFA} \propto -A_{\rm overlap}/d^4$), uniform periodic slot-tooth interdigitation ($A_{\rm overlap} = 0$, limited by single-scale evanescent screening at $\kappa \sim \pi /W_0$), and prefractal Cantor interdigitation ($W_k = W_1 b^{-(k-1)}$, stepped depths $H_k$, partitioning transverse fringing fields across separated wavenumber bands). \textbf {b}, Three-dimensional cutaway render of the four-fold symmetric ($C_4$, $90^\circ $ sector period) concentric gold rotor and stator in the disengaged open-slot state ($\theta = 3^\circ $). Downward-protruding concentric rotor teeth ($z \in [-100, 0]\text { nm}$, $H_1 = \CantorNtwoHybridrzHGenoneNm {}\text { nm}$, $H_2 = \CantorNtwoHybridrzHGentwoNm {}\text { nm}$) interdigitate radially inside thin slotted Cantor stator aperture rings ($25\text { nm}$ membrane thickness, $z \in [-25, 0]\text { nm}$) suspended above recessed azimuthal landing pads ($150\text { nm}$ thickness, top surface at $z = -115\text { nm}$) and supported by a four-spoke $\text {Si}\langle 110\rangle $ flexure suspension. \textbf {c},\textbf {d}, Cutaway renders and axial-radial $(r,z)$ cross-sections in (\textbf {c}) the disengaged open-slot state ($\theta = 0^\circ \text {--}6^\circ $, $A_{\rm overlap} = 0$, $F_z^{\rm PFA} = 0$, showing upward saddle-point repulsive force $F_z = +\roundtwo {\FractalNthreeCantorseventrackBemThetathreeFZPn }\text { pN}$ at $z_{\rm tip} = -100\text { nm}$ for $N=3$ on the \texttt {Standard} BEM mesh) and (\textbf {d}) the engaged landing-pad state ($\theta = 18^\circ \text {--}48^\circ $, $A_{\rm overlap} > 0$ across the $d = 15\text { nm}$ vertical gap, showing normal attraction $F_z = \roundtwo {\FractalNthreeCantorseventrackBemThetafoureightFZPn }\text { pN}$ for $N=3$). \textbf {e}, Radial cross-sectional profiles comparing the single-track baseline ($N=0$), first-generation slot ($N=1$), uniform periodic and monotonic controls, stepped $(r,z)$ $N=2$ Cantor ring, and seven-track $N=3$ Cantor ring across $r \in [0.30, 1.65]\ \mu \text {m}$}{figure.1}{}}
